# SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000196  -  CAT II
# The web server must only use forward proxies that route HTTP/2 requests
# upstream.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000196
group:           V-264366
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-002418
control_rev5:    SC-8

contribution:    Splunk can only state whether splunkd sends its own outbound requests
                 through a proxy and for which destinations, through server.conf
                 [proxyConfig] http_proxy, https_proxy, proxy_rules and no_proxy; it cannot
                 select the HTTP version used upstream.

external:        The forward proxy product, which decides whether it routes HTTP/2 requests
                 upstream
external:        The organizational determination of whether a forward proxy is used at
                 all, which triggers the check text's own not applicable clause

manual_reason:   The check text makes the requirement not applicable where no forward proxy
                 is used, and where one is used Splunk exposes no setting for the upstream
                 HTTP version: server.conf.spec:1201-1288 limits [proxyConfig] to naming a
                 proxy server and the destinations routed through it, and states that
                 splunkd supports only the HTTP CONNECT method for proxied HTTPS requests,
                 while enable_tls_proxy merely moves outbound TLS to the splunk-tlsd helper
                 for Splunk Telemetry and SplunkBase connections.

citation:        SRG-APP-000439-WSR-000196 check text; server.conf.spec:1201-1288
finding:         This requirement cannot be decided from Splunk configuration; where a
                 forward proxy is used, that proxy must be shown to route HTTP/2 requests
                 upstream.
